    "source": {
      "application": "Synthetic Landau example",
      "version": "2026-10-06",
      "context": "Synthetic classroom data: sampled Landau curve; not measured detector data or Poisson histogram counts.\nGenerating model: y = b + A/w * landau((x-mpv)/w), with unit-area mode-zero landau.\nTruth: b=0 V, A=150 V*keV, mpv=50 keV, w=5 keV (ROOT width convention).\nIndependent Gaussian noise: sigma_i=0.025*(1+i/101) V; i=0..100.\nNumPy PCG64 seed 20261006; NumPy 2.3.5, SciPy 1.17.0.\nGenerator: scripts/generate-landau-reference.py.\nReference: https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.stats.landau.html\nOpen landau.trksess for assigned uncertainties and starting values; or import the CSV,\nassign column 3 as Y uncertainty, enable advanced models, and select Landau peak.\nb starts fixed at zero. A is full-curve area, including the tail beyond these observations.",
      "fileName": "landau.csv"
    },
